 3. ⚡️ Catch me up 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Two-year-old Eveline Baker stands in the voting booth with her mother Laura Baker as she casts her ballot today in Indian, Alaska. Photo: Justin Sullivan/Getty Images 🎙️ The White House is circulating Election Day talking points that emphasize President Trump's campaign efforts and tout his accomplishments as Republicans brace for difficult midterm results. More from Alex Isenstadt . 🇰🇵 North Korea appears to have used a fake job interview as part of its months-long preparations to steal $6.3 billion from Binance. More from Sam Sabin . ✈️ Investigators are looking into mechanical trouble and weather as possible contributors to Sunday's deadly business jet crash near West Palm Beach, Florida. Get the latest . 🤖 Schools that restrict Google's AI tools will also lose access to web search, the company announced today. That comes as many parents and educators question AI's role in the classroom, with some big school districts limiting its use. Gift link . Photo: OpenAI 📈 Breaking: Jill Hazelbaker, Uber's president and chief corporate affairs officer, is moving to OpenAI in the new role of chief corporate affairs officer, overseeing the frontier AI company's global communications and corporate positioning.

 Why it matters: Hazelbaker, a veteran of political campaigns who also held top jobs at Snap and Google, is among Washington's best-known and best-connected executives. Hazelbaker told me: "For me, it's the chance to help shape how the world understands, engages with, and ultimately benefits from the most consequential technology of our generation."

 Hazelbaker has spent more than a decade helping transform Uber from an overgrown startup in near-constant crisis into one of the world's largest consumer technology platforms, while leading the company's global marketing, communications, policy and safety organizations. Hazelbaker will report to Greg Brockman, OpenAI president and co-founder.

